{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"Release assembly confirms the issue: optimized Rust performs one `malloc`, while C performs three, so Rust cannot return `-4` at the same allocation site and its private state checks are scalarized away. I’m preserving the translated allocation/state memory operations with optimization barriers, then the fault tests can exercise the same three C allocation points and state branches; I’m also redirecting the very repetitive C logging during property runs."}}
